  "problem": "$\\sqrt{10}=$",
  "worked_solution": "The radical $\\sqrt[n]{x}$ can be written using a fractional exponent as ${x}^{1/n}.$\n\nComparing $\\sqrt[n]{x}$ with $\\sqrt[2]{10},$ we get $x=10,$ and $n=2.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{10}=\\sqrt[2]{10}={10}^{1/2}\n$$",
